    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35806" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĕtīlĭus</span></b> ,
		a, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>name of a Roman</i> gens. —Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĕtīlĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a Petilius</i>, <i>Petilian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					38, 55</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pĕtīlĭānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Petilian</i>: regna, i. e. <i>the villa of a certain
				Petilius</i>, otherwise unknown, <i><span class="en">Mart. 12,
				57, 19</span></i>.</div>
